IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc2-prelim`
IMPORT `ssc2-factors`

-- Tests for ssc2-factors.l4 (ss 22, 23, 23A, 24). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.
-- Figures such as the lower earnings limit (100) and the upper earnings limit (800) are INVENTED test
-- inputs: the Act leaves them to regulations. Calendar facts used: 6 April 2010 was a Tuesday; Sunday
-- 11 April 2010 began the first week after it; 31 March 2024 was a Sunday (Easter Sunday); so was 30
-- March 2025 and so was 6 April 2025.

§ `Tests -- fixtures`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 22 test tax year beginning in` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS y

`s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770` MEANS `s 22(1)(a) Pay period` WITH
    `s 6 the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid in the pay period` IS 500
    `s 22(9) the upper earnings limit for the pay period` IS 770
    `s 22(4)(a) the contributions were paid at the reduced rate` IS FALSE
`s 22(1)(a) test period of 900 under a limit of 770` MEANS `s 22(1)(a) Pay period` WITH
    `s 6 the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid in the pay period` IS 900
    `s 22(9) the upper earnings limit for the pay period` IS 770
    `s 22(4)(a) the contributions were paid at the reduced rate` IS FALSE
`s 22(1)(a) test period of 600 at the reduced rate` MEANS `s 22(1)(a) Pay period` WITH
    `s 6 the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid in the pay period` IS 600
    `s 22(9) the upper earnings limit for the pay period` IS 770
    `s 22(4)(a) the contributions were paid at the reduced rate` IS TRUE

GIVEN pa IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS pa

§ `Tests -- s 22`

-- (9): weekly earner: the weekly limit; otherwise the prescribed equivalent, if supplied
#ASSERT `s 22(9) the limit that applies to the earnings` FALSE 800 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 22(9) the limit that applies to the earnings` TRUE 800 (JUST 3466) EQUALS JUST 3466
#ASSERT `s 22(9) the limit that applies to the earnings` TRUE 800 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 23(3)(a): earnings up to the limit count in full, the excess does not (both sides, and on the limit)
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(a) the amount to which the earnings factor from earnings equals or approximates` 500 770 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(a) the amount to which the earnings factor from earnings equals or approximates` 770 770 EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(a) the amount to which the earnings factor from earnings equals or approximates` 771 770 EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(a) the amount to which the earnings factor from earnings equals or approximates` 900 770 EQUALS 770

-- (4): reduced-rate primary contributions: no factor from 1987-88; and before it, no factor from reduced-rate
-- primary or from secondary Class 1 contributions. Secondary contributions yield no factor only before 1987.
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Subject to regulations under section 19(4) to (6)": if they provide otherwise, not covered
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(a): one pay period of a tax year from 1987-88
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the earnings factor derived from a pay period` `s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the earnings factor derived from a pay period` `s 22(1)(a) test period of 900 under a limit of 770` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST 770
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the earnings factor derived from a pay period` `s 22(1)(a) test period of 600 at the reduced rate` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the earnings factor derived from a pay period` `s 22(1)(a) test period of 600 at the reduced rate` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the first tax year the paragraph covers is 1987-88; 1986-87 is not covered by paragraph (a)
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the earnings factor derived from a pay period` `s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) FALSE EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the earnings factor derived from a pay period` `s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3)(b): Class 2 or Class 3: lower earnings limit times the number: 100 x 12 = 1200; none = 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(b) the amount to which the earnings factor from Class 2 or Class 3 contributions equals or approximates` 100 12 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(b) the amount to which the earnings factor from Class 2 or Class 3 contributions equals or approximates` 100 0 EQUALS 0

-- (1)(a) the year: two pay periods (500 and 770 after the cap) + (10 + 5 weeks) x 100 = 2770
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the annual earnings factor` (LIST `s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770`, `s 22(1)(a) test period of 900 under a limit of 770`) (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE 100 10 5 EQUALS JUST 2770
-- a reduced-rate period adds nothing: 500 + 0 + 1500 = 2000
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the annual earnings factor` (LIST `s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770`, `s 22(1)(a) test period of 600 at the reduced rate`) (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE 100 10 5 EQUALS JUST 2000
-- no pay periods: only the Class 2 and Class 3 weeks: 100 x (2 + 0) = 200
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the annual earnings factor` EMPTY (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) FALSE 100 2 0 EQUALS JUST 200
-- regulations may provide otherwise for reduced-rate earnings: not covered
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the annual earnings factor` (LIST `s 22(1)(a) test period of 600 at the reduced rate`) (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2000) TRUE 100 2 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- an earlier tax year is not under paragraph (a)
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(a) the annual earnings factor` (LIST `s 22(1)(a) test period of 500 under a limit of 770`) (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) FALSE 100 2 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(b): earlier years: 100 + 200 + 300 = 600
#ASSERT `s 22(1)(b) the annual earnings factor for an earlier tax year` 100 200 300 EQUALS 600

-- (2): the purposes
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` `s 22(2)(a) establishing entitlement to a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` `s 22(2)(a) establishing entitlement to a contributory employment and support allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` (`s 22(2)(a) establishing entitlement to a benefit specified in section 20(1)` `Category A retirement pension`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` (`s 22(2)(a) establishing entitlement to a benefit specified in section 20(1)` `short-term incapacity benefit`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "other than maternity allowance": the text's no
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` (`s 22(2)(a) establishing entitlement to a benefit specified in section 20(1)` `maternity allowance`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` `s 22(2)(b) calculating the additional pension in the rate of a long-term benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` `s 22(2)(c) establishing entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014, or calculating its rate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` `s 22(2)(d) establishing entitlement to bereavement support payment under section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the purpose is one for which earnings factors are treated as derived` `s 22(2) any other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2A): first appointed year or later: capped at the applicable limit; otherwise not covered
#ASSERT `s 22(2A) the earnings from which the earnings factor for additional pension is derived` TRUE 900 770 EQUALS JUST 770
#ASSERT `s 22(2A) the earnings from which the earnings factor for additional pension is derived` TRUE 770 770 EQUALS JUST 770
#ASSERT `s 22(2A) the earnings from which the earnings factor for additional pension is derived` TRUE 700 770 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 22(2A) the earnings from which the earnings factor for additional pension is derived` FALSE 900 770 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(2A) the subsection affects deemed earnings factors under sections 44A and 44B` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(2A) the subsection affects deemed earnings factors under sections 44A and 44B` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2B): before 2009-10 the upper earnings limit (here 800); from 2009-10 the upper accrual point (770)
#ASSERT `s 22(2B) the applicable limit` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2008) 800 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `s 22(2B) the applicable limit` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2009) 800 EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `s 22(2B) the applicable limit` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2015) 950 EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `s 22(2B) the applicable limit` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1990) 140 EQUALS 140

-- (3): the sources: 1987-88 on, and earlier years
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) `s 22(3)(a) earnings not exceeding the upper earnings limit on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) `s 22(3)(b) earnings which have been credited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) `s 22(3)(c) contributions of different classes paid or credited in the same tax year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) `s 22(3)(d) any combination of the methods in paragraphs (a) to (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1987) `s 22(3) contributions which have actually been paid, as opposed to those credited` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) `s 22(3)(c) contributions of different classes paid or credited in the same tax year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) `s 22(3) contributions which have actually been paid, as opposed to those credited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) `s 22(3)(a) earnings not exceeding the upper earnings limit on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(3) a separate earnings factor may be derived from the source` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1986) `s 22(3)(d) any combination of the methods in paragraphs (a) to (c)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5), (5ZA), (5ZB), (8)
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the person was credited with contributions or earnings by regulations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the person was credited with contributions or earnings by regulations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5) the person was credited with contributions or earnings by regulations` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZA) the person was credited by regulations toward a qualifying year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZA) the person was credited by regulations toward a qualifying year` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZB) the regulations must provide for crediting the person for the period` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZB) the regulations must provide for crediting the person for the period` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZB) the regulations must provide for crediting the person for the period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZB) the regulations must provide for crediting the person for the period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(5ZB) the regulations must provide for crediting the person for the period` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the allowance is a contributory employment and support allowance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(8) the allowance is a contributory employment and support allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 23`

-- (2): revalued factors for 1978-79 or later years need not be whole pounds; every other factor derived as in
-- s 22(1) "shall be expressed, subject to subsection (2) below, as whole numbers of pounds" (s 23(1)(a), src:808)
#ASSERT `s 23(2) subsection (1) requires the earnings factor to be expressed as a whole number of pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1978) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) subsection (1) requires the earnings factor to be expressed as a whole number of pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1990) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) subsection (1) requires the earnings factor to be expressed as a whole number of pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1977) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) subsection (1) requires the earnings factor to be expressed as a whole number of pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1990) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(a): revalued: as increased; otherwise the whole number the regulations' tables give; none given: not covered
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the earnings factor expressed in pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1990) 1234.56 TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1234.56
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the earnings factor expressed in pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1990) 1234.56 FALSE (JUST 1234) EQUALS JUST 1234
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the earnings factor expressed in pounds` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 1990) 1234.56 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3A): additional pension: upper accrual point from 2009-10, the upper earnings limit (here 800) before
#ASSERT `s 23(3A) the limit for subsection (3)(a) for the purpose of additional pension` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2008) 800 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `s 23(3A) the limit for subsection (3)(a) for the purpose of additional pension` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2009) 800 EQUALS 770

§ `Tests -- s 23A`

-- (1)(a) Category A: the contributor attains pensionable age on or after 6 April 2010
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2010)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category A retirement pension` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2010)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) Category B by virtue of section 48A or 48AA
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1)(b) payable by virtue of section 48A or 48AA` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2012)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1)(b) payable by virtue of section 48A or 48AA` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2010)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) Category B by virtue of section 48B: dies on or after that date without having attained pensionable age before it
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1)(c) payable by virtue of section 48B` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) (JUST (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1)(c) payable by virtue of section 48B` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) (JUST (Date 5 4 2010)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1)(c) payable by virtue of section 48B` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2010)) (JUST (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1)(c) payable by virtue of section 48B` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `Category B retirement pension` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (d) widowed parent's allowance: the contributor dies on or after 6 April 2010
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) (JUST (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) (JUST (Date 5 4 2010)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- any other benefit: not covered
#ASSERT `s 23A(1) this section applies to the benefit` `attendance allowance` `s 23A(1) payable by virtue of another section` (`s 23A test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2012)) (JUST (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3): a relevant carer in respect of a week
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (2): one credit for a Sunday-start week that begins after 6 April 2010 in which the person was a relevant carer
#ASSERT `s 23A(2) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the week` (Date 11 4 2010) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 23A(2) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the week` (Date 4 4 2010) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(2) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the week` (Date 12 4 2010) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(2) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the week` (Date 11 4 2010) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(2) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the week` (Date 11 4 2010) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5): 52 contributions for a tax year ending before 6 April 2010 (2009-10 ends 5 April 2010; 2010-11 does not)
#ASSERT `s 23A(5) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the tax year` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2009) TRUE EQUALS JUST 52
#ASSERT `s 23A(5) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the tax year` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2010) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(5) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the tax year` (`s 22 test tax year beginning in` 2005) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6), (7): 22 years for (1)(a) to (c); half the requisite number for (1)(d)
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `Category A retirement pension` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `Category B retirement pension` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `widowed parent's allowance` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 44) EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `widowed parent's allowance` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `widowed parent's allowance` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `widowed parent's allowance` NOTHING (JUST 44) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the maximum number of tax years that can be credited under subsection (5)` `maternity allowance` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 44) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23A(7) the requisite number of years from the table in paragraph 5(5) of Schedule 3` (JUST 44) EQUALS JUST 44
#ASSERT `s 23A(7) the requisite number of years from the table in paragraph 5(5) of Schedule 3` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the number of years actually credited: the lesser of the years at home and the maximum (both sides)
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the number of tax years for which the contributor is credited under subsection (5)` 10 (JUST 22) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the number of tax years for which the contributor is credited under subsection (5)` 22 (JUST 22) EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the number of tax years for which the contributor is credited under subsection (5)` 23 (JUST 22) EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 23A(6) the number of tax years for which the contributor is credited under subsection (5)` 23 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

